" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266532} {:answer/id #uuid "6f0dba1e-ebd9-58df-9ff0-a39f534c6156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267118} {:answer/id #uuid "9a78f2b9-be60-5dd9-a1b2-d3dae91c37e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267540} {:answer/id #uuid "a54496d0-737c-5f0e-b323-1106d3723e9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267634} {:answer/id #uuid "da3d8464-42f7-59e9-bbc9-ba3a5c255583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bba42d0-4d22-55d1-bf2a-5afa7f154545" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266532} :answer-field/id #uuid "464dd787-aac1-5fd3-8b68-a426f70499c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268525}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5d3c5f6c-be88-5a7d-88c2-f5f9124aa97d" :question/math-academy-id "q-13533" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269045 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "573778d5-04ef-570b-bb92-30f2581d353a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266920} {:answer/id #uuid "853703e3-5ee8-58a7-a762-0b6b51b9da3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267318} {:answer/id #uuid "8a690975-9629-524f-8754-019e655cbcf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267378} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e7245c-ae8f-576f-ad7b-ae3e6def801c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267761} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d49c16-cf0d-5d32-ac21-f912a3f35a4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5d49c16-cf0d-5d32-ac21-f912a3f35a4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267918} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8a52cc8-a59a-5790-8e07-7483e8b8eee9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268791}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f9af6a27-d8cc-5d10-84b4-1e204dd24944" :question/math-academy-id "q-13537" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi }$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $2\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(1-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297287 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4675341d-47de-58d1-9169-e4ea300f6534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295666} {:answer/id #uuid "49060b70-8ca0-5560-a25f-c33fdf13abe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295684} {:answer/id #uuid "73e82961-671e-5f43-927c-85b68cebb79e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295902} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc5e39c-b266-5cff-bbd7-b9a7c961e739" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296018} {:answer/id #uuid "902705ff-4eac-5fc0-8d8a-b9ebd4cdfeff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4675341d-47de-58d1-9169-e4ea300f6534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295666} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c5828d6-8af8-5472-82db-0c5fb62611d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296780}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7ade3ef7-2470-5279-802e-68d9ba79206f" :question/math-academy-id "q-3038" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡(1/x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡(1/x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8483f978-0eb7-58b8-8af7-e33b9170b809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8483f978-0eb7-58b8-8af7-e33b9170b809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318016} :answer-field/id #uuid "072ef757-3ef7-5291-a2b9-f78bdb72dd2b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318442}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b2f52a91-e2df-5743-9b16-3551c628a81b" :question/math-academy-id "q-350202" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}8xsec\\,(4{x}^{2})tan\\,(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=4{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=8x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi /3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}8xsec\\,(4{x}^{2})tan\\,(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}sec\\,(4{x}^{2})tan\\,(4{x}^{2})\\cdot 8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a0832f3-44e5-55dc-b0d6-cde9d7754977" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a0832f3-44e5-55dc-b0d6-cde9d7754977" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317931} :answer-field/id #uuid "81013bc8-e699-5fa8-92f3-108172fec02c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318703}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4977c738-ef65-5d72-9699-ec8683cb5818" :question/math-academy-id "q-350203" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=6{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=12x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=12x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /12}$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /2$ | $\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\cdot 12x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u)\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\  & =0-1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486542 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67db1928-5d77-5d01-9982-b91efb720baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\cot{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486547} {:answer/id #uuid "80b3b820-877a-56c3-86d8-db243bd28b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\csc{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486551} {:answer/id #uuid "8414f7a2-369f-5120-b9a8-467cd2cbffd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\cot{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486553} {:answer/id #uuid "8dcad831-351c-5fb6-8252-0ad06ca0e301" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\cot{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486554} {:answer/id #uuid "d2010a1d-48cd-5e3a-8bb6-9f30dbdd2492" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cot{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67db1928-5d77-5d01-9982-b91efb720baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\cot{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486547} :answer-field/id #uuid "240f4141-c6e4-573e-9f31-860c6fa6e3b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486545}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "002482ff-69a9-5b63-b3f0-5cd70a51819a" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2 x \\csc^{2}{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2 x \\csc^{2}{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x &= 1\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= - \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}+C \\\\ &= - \\cot{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486552 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b2b14aa-939d-5f78-95d5-a8ac2d5a46b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\cos{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486543} {:answer/id #uuid "1202f884-82b1-540e-bfd1-0ee80ba2c514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\cos{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486544} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b4275b-87e1-5689-822b-8dac3c858579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486558} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6699db-b1f0-5226-8168-b9ec448eac86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\cos{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486560} {:answer/id #uuid "fcef9471-29d4-56f5-9a65-4b6c75538bcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 \\cos{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b2b14aa-939d-5f78-95d5-a8ac2d5a46b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\cos{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486543} :answer-field/id #uuid "79c1360c-2029-597a-92dc-abe7f1cbfea3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486550}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82583355-6299-599e-bdc6-d65fa8aebd0a" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x &= 1\\int \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= - \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}+C \\\\ &= - \\cos{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486555 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28b0a88b-6033-5a60-beab-0cbad3f7fed3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\tan{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486546} {:answer/id #uuid "6f9bacea-3262-508b-9719-4fd80bf9d534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\sec{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486548} {:answer/id #uuid "79463279-bba4-5ce7-b66d-91ca6c29fee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\tan{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486549} {:answer/id #uuid "b44d88f2-1b54-541f-aa56-dae6e3f577f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\tan{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486556} {:answer/id #uuid "c04acc4c-98a0-5857-8fdc-cdb07ac37366" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\tan{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79463279-bba4-5ce7-b66d-91ca6c29fee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\tan{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486549} :answer-field/id #uuid "b59d98d5-6b64-56b9-afca-bffec0e1eaf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486557}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f181c0b-4ade-5cfb-806e-89c254367d4c" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 8 x^{2} \\sec^{2}{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^{3},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3 x^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8 x^{2} \\sec^{2}{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x &= \\frac{8}{3}\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= \\frac{8 \\tan{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}+C \\\\ &= \\frac{8 \\tan{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1536851e-467a-513f-a39f-a987ce9f476f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580419} {:answer/id #uuid "419eae3a-7c99-539d-9f8c-43bd5d3ee2ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580497} {:answer/id #uuid "57682a10-50f1-57c4-b856-6b7dcb623188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580531} {:answer/id #uuid "fb615c57-9a5f-515f-9538-4b290aa37b2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580784} {:answer/id #uuid "fd9a6454-9002-50d7-81dc-56d4699c4393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1536851e-467a-513f-a39f-a987ce9f476f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580419} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed6dccc4-202e-5529-b8af-ac630177fe14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580874}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "038974cd-ae48-5200-9bdc-eb592bd2ef40" :question/math-academy-id "q-13467" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{3}$, Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b4cd558-9e46-545e-9b83-95b0ce86e4f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580405} {:answer/id #uuid "1a0cd29b-2281-5fdf-b83a-3d81905f346b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580425} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff41e67-12fd-5ad3-95e3-b11f2dafd8a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580466} {:answer/id #uuid "3ae7711a-aefc-5cb7-b38b-ebf016041585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580486} {:answer/id #uuid "a1cd5e71-b7f5-5663-936f-68abc2dbf93c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ff41e67-12fd-5ad3-95e3-b11f2dafd8a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580466} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8e9515f-e4f9-5256-98c2-11c0b1c56ec8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580864}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "185fc978-acea-5e9e-aec8-3d21ff92c62e" :question/math-academy-id "q-13470" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{3})\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{3})\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{3})\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "399980b9-86fd-5875-909a-55ccdeec0bc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "399980b9-86fd-5875-909a-55ccdeec0bc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580483} :answer-field/id #uuid "2147e959-626e-5c5e-a384-3e369b129c13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580807}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "95f61cbe-50e0-52a1-9899-3308592615d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-350186" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /4}}8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=4{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=8x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /4}}8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /4}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4{x}^{2})\\cdot 8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580949 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "143b0cf4-599c-56a0-9697-0fd3b6ad7b6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580415} {:answer/id #uuid "2da5f0d2-90ae-5eae-81fe-3ad54334ae4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580460} {:answer/id #uuid "a609fb08-4df5-5f2f-b07c-716c4b0fa8c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580666} {:answer/id #uuid "c625891a-9893-5be4-8d26-dd89a0f3f09e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3{x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580696} {:answer/id #uuid "f6631fd8-eb98-5921-a11b-8cab13d33385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2da5f0d2-90ae-5eae-81fe-3ad54334ae4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580460} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cd33e1c-d19d-5110-b549-226f09fdc6db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580844}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8478693-7123-504b-ab62-3a7e2bce3f4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-13471" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 5{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186605837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5841f26e-e77f-5abf-8554-e49b74956114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605411} {:answer/id #uuid "ad4068a3-7725-577e-884c-b90d2c736c8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605570} {:answer/id #uuid "bb027bbd-ba2d-5754-a425-ba0860b0a7f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605592} {:answer/id #uuid "e0cf21a2-6ecf-507d-a9c4-69f7f0f50726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605661} {:answer/id #uuid "fab56faa-facf-50d9-bd7a-d52d97b81de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fab56faa-facf-50d9-bd7a-d52d97b81de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605708} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fb66e89-485f-5599-801d-5b503ee20e58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605721}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b7a1c4f-ee46-59c2-a0d1-028c953d1f17" :question/math-academy-id "q-13460" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186605847 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "084d6296-4e0e-5291-a90f-82b7617ff7a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605264} {:answer/id #uuid "2341f810-fcdd-5f61-be44-39e52dde1228" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605311} {:answer/id #uuid "320634f0-cac2-5787-bb32-88a333793829" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605344} {:answer/id #uuid "86afb790-2d4b-5953-a77a-737ee084b7a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605490} {:answer/id #uuid "a9fbf28e-c6bd-5a97-8692-75b54a26c81b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2341f810-fcdd-5f61-be44-39e52dde1228" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605311} :answer-field/id #uuid "d01f36ee-521c-54fe-9274-182cb22b18d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605813}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3d11b8d3-3d89-559d-9bb2-2df9905b80bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-13544" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /18}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /9}}2x{sec}^{2}⁡(3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /18}$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /9}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /18}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /9}}2x{sec}^{2}⁡(3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /18}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /9}}2{sec}^{2}⁡(3{x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}2{sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186611646 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16adda69-f89e-5bfd-af50-5b8bdb679010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{x})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611107} {:answer/id #uuid "35602054-babb-540a-9b9d-a91bf0cf7892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{x})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611150} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad15320-a1c5-5373-af1d-0273c9fbce64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{x})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611180} {:answer/id #uuid "96c61819-0fb7-50f0-b5d8-8d48e3ea6491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{x})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611307} {:answer/id #uuid "cff5f868-a0dd-5fc7-ad99-0ff5e51cab1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{x})}{\\sqrt{x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ad15320-a1c5-5373-af1d-0273c9fbce64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{x})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611180} :answer-field/id #uuid "447f0452-c7c0-5061-ac54-ed0e8121ebfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611488}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f8b1a93e-d361-59f6-a945-adc08b0914f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-2377" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{x})}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\sqrt{x}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,⟹\\,2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{x})}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{x})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00d572ac-01af-5955-82aa-3e768b36e2f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00d572ac-01af-5955-82aa-3e768b36e2f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657049} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6512d6a-335a-528d-b7fb-d8511385140d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657402}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1bf4d546-3968-549c-809c-efe4c07584b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-350883" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /30}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /10}}10xcsc\\,(5{x}^{2})cot\\,(5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=5{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=10x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=10x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /30}$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /10}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /30}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /10}}10xcsc\\,(5{x}^{2})cot\\,(5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /30}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /10}}csc\\,(5{x}^{2})cot\\,(5{x}^{2})\\cdot 10x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(u)\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)) \\\\  & =-(1-2) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186658964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0007f85e-299c-5b79-b9ec-8453687d1ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658407} {:answer/id #uuid "18a80f2e-bcd8-593d-984d-a492d040e259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658435} {:answer/id #uuid "35a285de-59a9-5b2f-88de-9dae11d3c597" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658482} {:answer/id #uuid "aea7e1e8-b929-5225-a1c2-e230e26ee364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658660} {:answer/id #uuid "d78244c3-8175-5680-ae70-38b7480692ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aea7e1e8-b929-5225-a1c2-e230e26ee364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658660} :answer-field/id #uuid "5769a818-a51d-5cb6-b9be-b957cdd1a61a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658851}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "afb796da-b0f3-583a-9b91-f7ceb9e49619" :question/math-academy-id "q-13469" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2{x}^{2}{csc}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}{csc}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2{csc}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2{csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\int {csc}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186658981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26428b0f-27ad-57ff-82c1-38411c7ad4e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658459} {:answer/id #uuid "64009f61-39d7-5a4c-87a5-147048718d28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658555} {:answer/id #uuid "88560ed4-3fd2-5e35-b823-59a0de90bf5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658598} {:answer/id #uuid "9d479de0-2368-5b17-a3d1-550085306fdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658634} {:answer/id #uuid "d4866fef-c958-566f-bda6-62f7eafd4907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26428b0f-27ad-57ff-82c1-38411c7ad4e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658459} :answer-field/id #uuid "73c3d111-7c51-5bd3-8a2a-34f907747af7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186658862}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cd35717b-5994-5159-928f-a06c0623a4c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-13463" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{2})\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{2})\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{2})\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Products Containing Trigonometric Functions Using Substitution"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068918 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068570 :question/id #uuid "03e461a3-0fe0-5fb5-813e-ae23a5dc606a" :question/math-academy-id "e-467" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/4} \\dfrac{\\tan x \\sec^2 x}{1+\\tan^2x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator, because\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(1+\\tan^2 x) = 2\\tan{x}\\sec^2 x.\n$$\n\nSo, let $u = 1+\\tan^2 x.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} u}{\\textrm{d}x } = 2\\tan x\\sec^2 x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u = \\tan x\\sec^2 x\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi/4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc24eade-1b3d-5672-88fd-0bb48b371509" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487553 :question-generator/id #uuid "8808b3a8-f5d2-5df4-bd7b-4bc3ba403cda" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186068918.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86e493cf-4eca-5e4c-80d2-77afb41f75fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + \\sqrt{2} - \\ln 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065452} {:answer/id #uuid "9165ce54-93c6-51e3-8558-20f309c69be9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (1 + \\sqrt{2}) - \\ln 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065453} {:answer/id #uuid "0344248e-4755-5685-a633-05cc9a0872eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (1 + \\sqrt{2}) + \\ln 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065454} {:answer/id #uuid "6e6c0845-9461-5d57-a858-7ed83c05ef06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (1 - \\sqrt{2}) + \\ln 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065455} {:answer/id #uuid "7279b708-b196-52f0-9a24-096cbe3995a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (1 - \\sqrt{2}) - \\ln 2" :db/id #edb/ref 175921