(2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235967} {:answer/id #uuid "76b6ae8e-c79f-55ba-a4ee-eefbd27a16dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2))-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236561} {:answer/id #uuid "a2d45765-acec-5856-a6ab-e36b05832cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236838} {:answer/id #uuid "cc183065-84cd-56eb-a1d1-9d2feb89fa08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237113} {:answer/id #uuid "f48fc14e-d981-58be-9dc4-626252e8ef41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2))-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc183065-84cd-56eb-a1d1-9d2feb89fa08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237113} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e59f25-dfe5-5cac-9866-d5a810c20c90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237513}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1f3bfc39-323e-5886-ac57-446859b38bb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-10045" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator, because\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nSo, let $u=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)$ | $1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21e3ecae-eebb-5e3a-a11b-f0a963c45845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247724} {:answer/id #uuid "40e20505-16c6-5378-838a-6646518a5bbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247998} {:answer/id #uuid "4c791187-2258-52f5-98d9-f31bd89f2b7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248106} {:answer/id #uuid "c006ff4f-d73f-524e-9036-74de891bcd97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249131} {:answer/id #uuid "e4fe0ff3-3d1e-517d-9ef9-18da948a5fd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4fe0ff3-3d1e-517d-9ef9-18da948a5fd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249441} :answer-field/id #uuid "dee454e9-5772-5a92-9bc2-c3b4bcce16d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250054}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cf1ad1f8-f4e6-5785-9ed6-ccc3fe200091" :question/math-academy-id "q-113998" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2}\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1334b7fa-d127-5c64-b002-27ad26e5060d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1334b7fa-d127-5c64-b002-27ad26e5060d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319444} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2b3eddf-4c98-5452-9b07-9d55d5e1acb3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320676}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f99bfe31-a733-5730-90f9-a01fb52dbe70" :question/math-academy-id "q-350887" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u={sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4af3f687-0fd5-5613-b369-2c62699adfdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}\\left(\\frac{6}{5}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4af3f687-0fd5-5613-b369-2c62699adfdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}\\left(\\frac{6}{5}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319615} :answer-field/id #uuid "388b5a6e-6419-5e60-a343-6344e34c07b9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320295}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "efdb53cf-5359-5a73-8752-5be46ae654bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-350901" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5)=-24{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nSo, differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-24{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /3$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $6$ | $5$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\cdot 24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{5}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{6}^{5}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{6}^{5} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡6) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{6}{5}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320751 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fb74e6d-27ba-5dab-9bc3-14bcd6aca19d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319487} {:answer/id #uuid "bf2617d8-6d99-5cd0-a36b-cb5a85fa00c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf2617d8-6d99-5cd0-a36b-cb5a85fa00c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429919} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb778354-29e8-5b6b-9ab2-f74bbde5e184" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320651}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8cafdf18-d2d8-5608-a2ba-c48b80df9a64" :question/math-academy-id "q-350904" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x),$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\cdot (\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{4}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{4}^{3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342058 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ebec160-c5ac-548d-a451-e22560d5e12b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339843} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8992b4-908e-5460-ac2b-f416bb5dc366" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340237} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5a7820-a12c-5bfc-bde4-617efde18d2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340408} {:answer/id #uuid "cab5ae41-b98b-5ba7-a67b-473710627bc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340922} {:answer/id #uuid "cd94d4a2-ccc1-5dba-be7a-60f4ca899cad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd94d4a2-ccc1-5dba-be7a-60f4ca899cad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340953} :answer-field/id #uuid "d39a8b1c-171e-529f-bad2-ef340a8e19a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341755}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0b965c69-7854-507b-827e-0b6fbbb52fef" :question/math-academy-id "q-73674" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator, because\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}))=2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSo, let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})}\\cdot (y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e5262af-da0e-5a59-8704-7c9dacf4de2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{2}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429914} {:answer/id #uuid "9f63075a-1c8a-5a7b-92d3-a38ee960a89e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429916} {:answer/id #uuid "9fd0f034-ce27-5ace-8026-4eaf6cb1ce68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429917} {:answer/id #uuid "f18bdd3d-8085-5e2e-822e-62d75b040c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429923} {:answer/id #uuid "f602ed78-2e15-5cdc-81a3-3dc36a33f074" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f63075a-1c8a-5a7b-92d3-a38ee960a89e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429916} :answer-field/id #uuid "5edcce3e-e53a-5f19-ab28-fc88ce15b3a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429926}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "305ab7d8-b9f8-5861-8b01-dd9a503b80df" :question/math-academy-id "q-113997" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1}\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}(u-1)\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int (1-\\frac{1}{u})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =u-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=C+1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487529 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23cf7ff8-ac0a-583b-9194-64e241ac34ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\ln|\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487525} {:answer/id #uuid "2f886dbf-5e77-59c5-b9f8-0d0800987e35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\ln|\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487526} {:answer/id #uuid "6c032907-c215-5c0a-8b01-3af3123417e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\ln|\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487535} {:answer/id #uuid "74a107be-c47e-5e9f-a02e-5aacc9f7ae55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\ln|\\cos{\\left(x \\righ